<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Durango (city)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1563">1563</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Victoria de Durango</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Durango, officially Victoria de Durango, is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, capital of the state of Durango. It was founded in 1563 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-ibarra">Francisco de Ibarra</a> as the capital of the province of Nueva <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biscay">Vizcaya</a>, named after his native Biscay, and lies beside the Cerro de Mercado, a large hill of iron ore. Its colonial cathedral and the surrounding desert landscapes, used in many Western films, are well known.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/durango-city.jpg" alt="Durango (city)" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Microstar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montage_Victoria_de_Durango.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
